From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:30:00 +0000
Subject: drm/sun4i: mixer: Run the H616 display engine at 696 MHz

The vendor BSP clocks the H616 display engine at 696 MHz (pll-de and
de). At 600 MHz a 4096x2160 mode at 60 Hz (594 MHz pixel clock, 304
pixels of horizontal blanking) has too little margin: while the video
engine decodes a 4K stream, TCON TV0 reports FIFO underflows about
twice a second and the TV shows bands of displaced lines. At 696 MHz
there are no underflows under the same load.

Use the vendor's rate.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c
@@ -1938,7 +1938,7 @@
 
 static const struct sun8i_mixer_cfg sun50i_h616_mixer0_cfg = {
 	.de_type	= SUN8I_MIXER_DE33,
-	.mod_rate	= 600000000,
+	.mod_rate	= 696000000,
 	.has_formatter	= 1,
 };
 
